1
00:00:10,870 --> 00:00:13,330
If we develop this land merely
into a commercial complex,

2
00:00:13,330 --> 00:00:14,750
the total investment would be 5 billion,

3
00:00:14,750 --> 00:00:17,480
and our annual returns
would be around 1 billion.

4
00:00:17,550 --> 00:00:18,640
But if

5
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:23,430
we turn it into a theme park

6
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:24,830
and add twice the original investment,

7
00:00:24,830 --> 00:00:27,070
the overall visitor traffic
from the entertainment complex

8
00:00:27,070 --> 00:00:29,660
could boost our annual returns
by roughly five times.

9
00:00:29,660 --> 00:00:30,590
That's

10
00:00:31,960 --> 00:00:33,030
5 billion.

11
00:00:33,790 --> 00:00:35,340
5 billion!

12
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:40,060
The development blueprint for
Xingji Entertainment Complex

13
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:41,870
will undergo major revisions.

14
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:45,240
We have decided to add an investment

15
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:46,940
six times the original amount

16
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:49,280
to build a theme park
in the complex's core area.

17
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:51,640
Total investment: 30 billion.

18
00:00:54,980 --> 00:00:55,980
30 billion!

19
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:24,090
The highly anticipated Wen Group

20
00:01:22,470 --> 00:01:30,700
[Groundbreaking Ceremony for
Wen Group Xingji Theme Park]

21
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:25,789
Xingji Theme Park project

22
00:01:25,789 --> 00:01:27,520
held its groundbreaking ceremony today.

23
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:30,000
Group Chairman Wen Yanhui
attended in person, appearing alongside

24
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,000
his granddaughter Wen Jianan,
who made the move

25
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:33,970
from the entertainment industry
into business.

26
00:01:33,970 --> 00:01:36,710
Together, they turned the first shovelfuls
of soil for the project.

27
00:01:36,710 --> 00:01:37,509
Ms. Wen,

28
00:01:37,759 --> 00:01:39,000
these are the antiques we've handpicked,

29
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,430
we've handpicked,

30
00:01:41,150 --> 00:01:43,280
and they're best suited to your needs.

31
00:01:43,950 --> 00:01:45,009
Please take a look.

32
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:49,920
Wonderful.

33
00:01:51,759 --> 00:01:54,250
Yesterday, a batch of well-preserved
cultural relics

34
00:01:52,250 --> 00:02:00,830
[Wen Group Construction Site: Well-Preserved
Cultural Relics Unearthed Unexpectedly]

35
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:56,810
was unexpectedly discovered at the
construction site of a Wen Group project.

36
00:01:56,810 --> 00:01:57,700
This incident

37
00:01:57,759 --> 00:02:00,200
has undoubtedly cast a shadow over

38
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:01,260
Xingji Theme Park.

39
00:02:01,550 --> 00:02:02,350
Chairman Wen,

40
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:04,950
construction has halted after relics

41
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:07,230
were found on site.

42
00:02:11,620 --> 00:02:12,940
When can work resume?

43
00:02:13,510 --> 00:02:15,080
Officials from the Cultural
Relics Bureau said

44
00:02:15,080 --> 00:02:17,310
they cannot confirm the scale
of the excavation,

45
00:02:17,310 --> 00:02:19,400
so the project has to be
suspended temporarily.

46
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:20,800
What do you mean, cannot confirm?

47
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:23,630
A 30-billion project gets
suspended just like that?

48
00:02:23,630 --> 00:02:25,020
Go find a solution immediately!

49
00:02:25,020 --> 00:02:26,560
[Dearest, Episode 16]

50
00:02:25,270 --> 00:02:26,070
Okay.

51
00:02:28,690 --> 00:02:30,020
I said it from the start.

52
00:02:30,310 --> 00:02:31,540
A theme park carries

53
00:02:31,630 --> 00:02:32,400
far too many risks.

54
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:34,190
What's the point of bringing that up now?

55
00:02:34,190 --> 00:02:35,560
We've already poured in upfront capital.

56
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:37,490
We haven't seen any returns at all.

57
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:38,630
Let me be clear.

58
00:02:38,650 --> 00:02:40,310
If this project falls through,

59
00:02:40,310 --> 00:02:42,870
all our funds will go down the drain.

60
00:02:43,010 --> 00:02:44,400
Who said it's going to waste?

61
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:47,400
I've led Wen Group through decades
of market competition.

62
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:48,840
I have never failed.

63
00:02:48,860 --> 00:02:50,790
And this time will be no different.

64
00:02:52,870 --> 00:02:56,310
Chairman Wen has devoted
decades to Wen Group.

65
00:02:56,430 --> 00:02:59,400
Every crisis, he turned the tide.

66
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:01,360
No one could've predicted

67
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:04,160
relics would be dug up at Xingji.

68
00:03:04,240 --> 00:03:07,280
Everyone, stay calm.

69
00:03:07,310 --> 00:03:09,570
Chairman Wen will figure something out.

70
00:03:10,030 --> 00:03:11,430
Exactly.

71
00:03:12,230 --> 00:03:16,760
Chairman Wen, word has it you tried
to bribe the Cultural Relics Bureau,

72
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:19,710
but they wouldn't budge.

73
00:03:19,850 --> 00:03:22,250
So what's your plan now?

74
00:03:26,890 --> 00:03:29,770
Fellow shareholders, please stay calm.

75
00:03:50,329 --> 00:03:52,090
There will be a turning point.

76
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:56,360
A turning point? Ms. Wen.

77
00:03:56,630 --> 00:03:58,280
Anyone can talk big.

78
00:03:58,880 --> 00:04:00,830
If you really resolve this mess,

79
00:04:01,120 --> 00:04:03,560
I'd even call you my father.

80
00:04:11,490 --> 00:04:13,460
Authorities confirmed:

81
00:04:13,650 --> 00:04:16,450
The relics unearthed at Xingji
construction site

82
00:04:16,470 --> 00:04:19,180
were left behind years ago by
an anonymous collector,

83
00:04:19,180 --> 00:04:21,370
not an ancient ruin.

84
00:04:21,640 --> 00:04:24,080
The group's crisis is lifted.

85
00:04:24,390 --> 00:04:25,050
Great news!

86
00:04:25,630 --> 00:04:26,630
It's settled!

87
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:28,510
Mr. Li,

88
00:04:29,640 --> 00:04:32,159
do you still stand by what you just said?

89
00:04:32,310 --> 00:04:33,159
Wait —

90
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:38,680
Ms. Wen,

91
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:40,680
you really pulled off a miracle.

92
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:43,310
I knew it.

93
00:04:43,310 --> 00:04:46,240
Nothing's impossible with Ms. Wen
at the helm.

94
00:04:47,510 --> 00:04:49,090
Like grandfather, like granddaughter.

95
00:04:49,090 --> 00:04:51,920
The Wen family has a worthy successor.

96
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:54,159
Absolutely.

97
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:56,159
Fellow shareholders,

98
00:04:56,159 --> 00:04:58,560
Chairman Wen has guided us for years,

99
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:02,360
building Wen Group into what it is today.

100
00:05:02,390 --> 00:05:04,160
We ought to show respect.

101
00:05:05,050 --> 00:05:06,400
Indeed.

102
00:05:06,610 --> 00:05:08,610
Chairman Wen has made
extraordinary contributions.

103
00:05:08,610 --> 00:05:09,790
That's for sure.

104
00:05:09,810 --> 00:05:12,930
Without him, there would be no Wen Group.

105
00:05:14,240 --> 00:05:15,360
Nevertheless,

106
00:05:16,870 --> 00:05:18,780
on the Xingji project,

107
00:05:19,870 --> 00:05:22,680
Chairman Wen made a flawed call,

108
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,310
costing the group substantial losses.

109
00:05:27,430 --> 00:05:29,270
Grandfather is advanced in age.

110
00:05:29,360 --> 00:05:32,920
It's understandable that his judgment
on the project slipped.

111
00:05:33,310 --> 00:05:35,830
Still, I believe

112
00:05:36,270 --> 00:05:38,040
when it comes to Xingji,

113
00:05:38,270 --> 00:05:41,600
we should reconsider

114
00:05:42,100 --> 00:05:45,010
who should steer Wen Group
toward the future.

115
00:05:53,050 --> 00:05:56,640
As a member of the board of directors,

116
00:05:57,190 --> 00:05:59,770
I formally propose, in accordance with
the articles of association,

117
00:05:59,770 --> 00:06:01,800
to initiate board restructuring

118
00:06:05,900 --> 00:06:07,960
and hold a new election for Chairman.

119
00:06:13,650 --> 00:06:15,800
Well said! Hear, hear!

120
00:06:16,330 --> 00:06:17,010
Well said!

121
00:06:46,190 --> 00:06:47,040
Hao,

122
00:06:47,659 --> 00:06:50,500
I've reached the coastal path.

123
00:06:50,590 --> 00:06:51,520
Where are you?

124
00:06:51,750 --> 00:06:53,070
Follow the trail.

125
00:06:54,060 --> 00:06:55,790
You'll see a viewing platform.

126
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:56,920
I see it.

127
00:06:57,050 --> 00:06:57,530
Good.

128
00:06:57,830 --> 00:06:58,830
Wait for me there.

129
00:07:00,060 --> 00:07:00,900
Hurry up.

130
00:07:00,930 --> 00:07:01,460
Alright.

131
00:07:27,430 --> 00:07:28,160
Let this

132
00:07:28,970 --> 00:07:30,320
stay with you for now.

133
00:07:34,870 --> 00:07:35,670
Thank you.

134
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:00,920
Go!

135
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:03,410
Proceed to the wedding as planned.

136
00:08:05,940 --> 00:08:06,980
My bride.

137
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:11,900
Reclaim everything that belongs to you.

138
00:08:11,960 --> 00:08:14,990
Take back what's yours.

139
00:08:30,120 --> 00:08:30,920
Boring.

140
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:53,240
Wen Jianan!

141
00:08:52,690 --> 00:08:57,110
♪ In the darkness
where there is no light ♪

142
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:56,570
Happy birthday!

143
00:08:59,160 --> 00:09:04,160
♪ At the end of every lonely night ♪

144
00:09:05,850 --> 00:09:11,120
♪ Now my heart is beating once again ♪

145
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:17,810
♪ Finally I'm breathing past the pain ♪

146
00:09:19,580 --> 00:09:22,700
♪ In the winter breeze,
I feel your breath ♪

147
00:09:22,740 --> 00:09:26,430
♪ Waking up my soul from frozen death ♪

148
00:09:26,620 --> 00:09:33,670
♪ Like a miracle, you came in view ♪

149
00:09:33,700 --> 00:09:40,280
♪ At the edge of this breaking world ♪

150
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:44,520
♪ You are the only one
who brought the light ♪

151
00:09:44,960 --> 00:09:47,670
♪ Because it's you ♪

152
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:49,200
I knew you were alive.

153
00:09:47,710 --> 00:09:49,210
♪ All my sorrows ♪

154
00:09:49,280 --> 00:09:54,440
♪ Fading out of sight ♪

155
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:53,600
I will never leave you again.

156
00:09:54,460 --> 00:10:01,320
♪ In your arms, I'm born again and new ♪

157
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:07,040
♪ Holding tightly to my hands and scars ♪

158
00:10:08,660 --> 00:10:10,980
♪ Your deep breathing ♪

159
00:10:11,010 --> 00:10:15,010
♪ Guided like the stars ♪

160
00:10:15,290 --> 00:10:18,690
♪ Now I'll never let you go ♪

161
00:10:19,790 --> 00:10:21,120
He ran away in the night.

162
00:10:21,390 --> 00:10:22,550
Sorry, Miss.

163
00:10:22,810 --> 00:10:24,010
I failed to keep watch.

164
00:10:24,010 --> 00:10:25,360
I've already sent people to search.

165
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:26,120
No need.

166
00:10:27,320 --> 00:10:29,450
Yesterday was Wen Jianan's birthday.

167
00:10:29,750 --> 00:10:31,780
He must have gone back to her side.

168
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:34,810
Keep tracking them.

169
00:10:35,270 --> 00:10:38,240
I want updates on every
single move they make.

170
00:10:38,870 --> 00:10:39,630
Understood.
